# Reuse of the derivation of equal ground predicates within one satisfy
# call (TCMisc.sat, replaySolvedBinds): a Generic-representation
# traversal with a catch-all instance, over nested structs whose fields
# repeat a few types, derives the traversal of a field type once per
# satisfy call and replays it for the other field occurrences, under the
# dictionary ids and type variables the walk would draw.

# The traversal computes the same value with the shared dictionaries
test_c_veri DictSharing

# The mechanism: -trace-tc-dict-share prints one line per satisfy call
# that replayed a derivation (two for a definition, whose predicates are
# solved once while its body is checked and once more by tiExpl), with
# the counter numbers the replays drew, and the typecheck dump holds the
# same bindings as the derivation without reuse: one Generic dictionary
# per field occurrence (585), since a hit replays the recorded bindings
# instead of deriving them
compile_pass DictSharing.bs {-trace-tc-dict-share -dtypecheck=typecheck_%p.out} 1
find_n_strings typecheck_DictSharing.out {:: Prelude.Generic } 585
find_n_strings DictSharing.bs.bsc-out {satisfy: 80 derivations recorded, 21 replayed, 20802 counter numbers drawn by the replays} 2

# A small definition: the pinned line counts the ground predicates the
# call recorded, the later occurrences that replayed them and the
# numbers the replays drew
compile_pass DictSharingTrace.bs {-trace-tc-dict-share} 1
find_n_strings DictSharingTrace.bs.bsc-out {satisfy: 19 derivations recorded, 2 replayed, 54 counter numbers drawn by the replays} 2

# A replay leaves the typechecked program and the fresh-name counter
# where the walk would have left them: the typecheck dump of that
# definition, and the sequence of counter draws -trace-tcvar prints for
# the package, are the files the compiler without this reuse writes
# (both .expected files were written by that compiler, the dump with
# its trailing whitespace trimmed, which compare_file ignores); a reuse
# that drew other numbers for the replayed bindings would renumber
# every _tcdictN and _tctyvarN after the first hit
compile_pass DictSharingTrace.bs {-dtypecheck=typecheck_%p.out} 1
compare_file typecheck_DictSharingTrace.out
compile_pass DictSharingTrace.bs {-trace-tcvar} 1
compare_file DictSharingTrace.bs.bsc-out tcvar_DictSharingTrace.bsc-out.expected

# Never shared: a recursive or an incoherent result.  The recursive-Bits
# error (T0115) keeps its position and the incoherent-match diagnostics
# their count; see bsc.compile/letrec, bsc.typechecker/deriving
# (RecDeriveStructManyFields) and bsc.typechecker/typeclasses/coherence.

# A ground goal solved inside a partial reduction that satisfy puts aside
# is dropped with it (its bindings were solved under a substitution the
# retry does not keep), so a later equal predicate derives its own
compile_pass DictSharingRetry.bs {-trace-tc-dict-share} 1
find_n_strings DictSharingRetry.bs.bsc-out {satisfy:} 0
